                    insight_converged:      `Demonstrable convergence: you matched mechanisms to tacit know-how AND aligned with both HQ and the family, so transfer actually lifted performance. The DPMO and productivity gaps are closing on a fundable, staffable plan — HQ keeps local management.`,
                    insight_fragile:        `You hit the convergence target, but the foundation is thin — transfer or alignment is lagging. The number looks credible to the COO today, yet without both pillars it is fragile and likely to stall.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of demonstrable convergence. HQ executes the management-replacement option and flies in an expatriate team. Re-examine which barrier you left unaddressed — most likely you moved volume without alignment, or codified the tacit.`,
                    insight_noalign:        `You moved know-how but never aligned with HQ and the family. Kiessling's finding is blunt: transfer without strategic alignment does not lift performance — the family resistance capped your convergence.`,
